Hi gang,

I posted a few days ago - "Barbarian, early game strategy"

I took your advice.  I stopped trying to play the protection game (was
previously letting my pet kill almost everything).  I hauled a bunch
of stuff (from the mines and the dungeons) to an altar and tested.
Took my time and am very happy to report that I have ...

+4 small shield (original, +1 enchantment)
+3 splint mail (bought at shop)
+3 iron shoes
+2 helm
+0 gauntlets of power (bought at shop)
+0 cloak of invisibility

AC: -14   woo hoo!  This is record for me.

I ran into a bones file, got a cursed Mjollnir.  Spent some time
collecting scrolls, trying to price ID enchant armor and remove
curse.  Got 'em!  Rookie mistake when I read remove curse without
wielding Mjollnir.  I got the message but something else in my inv had
the curse removed.  Luck was on my side, must have been the luckstone
that I got at Mine's End, because I had another remove curse scroll in
my inv.  Wielded Mjollnir, read the scroll, good stuff.

I found a magic lamp, rubbed it before blessing it, released a djinni,
but no wish.  :-(  The djinni just walks around minetown now.

I completed Sokoban and got a bag of holding.  The treasure zoo was
incredibly easy.  I was worried about a monster with a dangerous wand,
but I got the bag and went back to the dungeon.

Now, to my request for advice ... I'm on Level 12 of the main
dungeon.  I just successfully converted an altar to be co-aligned.
I've got a blessed clear potion and am wondering what to bless.

amulet: ESP
scrolls: enchant armor, identify, teleport, earth, several unid'ed
potion: full healing, several unidentified
rings: sustain ability, see invisible, +1 gain constitution
wands: digging, create monster, striking, several unid'ed
items: unicorn horn, bag of holding, leash, towel, lamp
gems: luckstone

I'm leaning toward the unicorn horn (based on what I've read).  Thanks
in advance!




